# UTF-8 negotiation (issues/lsp-position-encoding-is-negotiated-against-the-clients-list.md):
# the client offers ONLY utf-8 in general.positionEncodings, so the server
# answers positionEncoding: utf-8 (never an encoding the client did not
# offer) and converts every column to/from BYTE offsets. Line 1 of the
# document carries an astral-plane rune (the emoji is four UTF-8 bytes, two
# UTF-16 units, one rune) before the identifiers: hover at the BYTE column
# of y (19) answers, at 18 it does not (compare lsp-position-encoding-utf16,
# same shape at UTF-16 columns 17/16). documentSymbol answers the FLAT
# SymbolInformation shape - this client declares no
# hierarchicalDocumentSymbolSupport.
timeout=240
framing=strict
